the variable that has the dconstraint "distribution" should only take
values either 0 or 1 where the value is 1 if the constraint is active.
I think this is what we say in the manual but let me know if you see
that we said it could be in [0,1] anywhere!

I'm not sure what you're trying to do with the 0.8 values. If you want
the constraint to be mu[i] > 0.8, just put the 0.8 in  as
"dconstraint( mu [i] > 0.8)".

Chris

