Hi,

 I'm a new Nimble user and currently I am working on a state space model problem based on ensemble of states. So, I have an approximate loglikelihood function LK(data_vec, param_vec,...) [it has arguments of different types like arma mat, arma vec etc] that is written in Rcpp/RcppArmadillo and compiled thereafter. Priors of the parameters (param_vec) are pretty clearly defined and I can add them in the nimbleCode() . However, I am wondering if it is possible to incorporate the loglik function in the nimble framework.

Thanks,
Subhomoy

From udd632bd3bbcdd7e9 at groups.google.com  Thu Feb  8 08:20:08 2018
