Hi All,

I'm trying to make sure my WAIC is calculated properly. Adding monitors with addMonitors() changes the WAIC result. Can anyone explain what's going on there? I had a look at [https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimble/blob/57bc1b57d3770b4d16f2530390c06a6ce66d8186/packages/nimble/R/MCMC_build.R] and [https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/nimble/versions/0.6-8/topics/configureMCMC], but I'm still a bit confused. I know the mvSamples are being used, and that top-level stochastic nodes are used to simulate everything down the chain. But, what, precisely, happens to the calculation when an additional node (downstream stochastic or deterministic) is added to monitors? I can't quite tell from the code and man page.

Any insights would be helpful.

